gress"},{"to":"e_0de476f32852","type":"shared_country","evidence":"Both concern United States and are classed as Geopolitics","method":"shared country + category","confidence":0.5,"observed":true,"title":"Trump issues order to bypass Russian sanctions in bill named for late Lindsey Graham"},{"to":"e_107ff6d6edd9","type":"shared_country","evidence":"Both concern United States and are classed as Geopolitics","method":"shared country + category","confidence":0.5,"observed":true,"title":"Trump waives Graham Act sanctions ahead of Rubio’s India visit"},{"to":"e_1dce637bc856","type":"shared_country","evidence":"Both concern United States and are classed as Geopolitics","method":"shared country + category","confidence":0.5,"observed":true,"title":"Getting paid by Putin : Democrats criticise Trump waiver of sanctions under Lindsey Graham Act"},{"to":"e_bf89b525b1cf","type":"shared_country","evidence":"Both concern United States and are classed as Geopolitics","method":"shared country + category","confidence":0.5,"observed":true,"title":"Trump’s Russia sanctions reversal deepens rift with Zelensky as Europe rallies behind Kyiv"}],"revisions":[],"entities":[{"name":"Russia","kind":"place","mentions":8},{"name":"Graham Act","kind":"person","mentions":3},{"name":"Congress","kind":"organisation","mentions":2},{"name":"Graham Law","kind":"person","mentions":1},{"name":"India","kind":"place","mentions":1},{"name":"Russian","kind":"group","mentions":1},{"name":"Trump Waives Russia Sanctions","kind":"organisation","mentions":1},{"name":"Ukraine","kind":"place","mentions":1}],"disputes":[],"summary":{"text":"On October 17, 2026, President Trump waived some sanctions and restrictions on Russia, including tariffs, under a new law called the Graham Act. This action was part of a broader effort to ease economic pressure on Russia, which had been involved in conflicts with Ukraine. The decision was made to align with the interests of the United States during midterm elections.","text_hi":null,"model":"qwen2.5-1.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf","created_at":"2026-10-17T07:02:23Z"},"context":{"background":[{"title":"International sanctions during the Russian invasion of Ukraine","extract":"Following the full declaration of the Russian invasion of Ukraine, which started on 24 February 2022, institutions such as the United States, the European Union, and other Western countries introduced or significantly expanded sanctions covering Russian president Vladimir Putin, other government members and Russian citizens in general. Some Russian banks were banned from using the SWIFT international payments system. The sanctions and the boycotts of Russia and Belarus have impacted the Russian economy in various ways. Nevertheless, Russian authorities have mitigated the impact of sanctions by procuring essential goods from consumer products that are rarely subject to export restrictions, by exploiting globalized supply chains, and by turning toward trading partners who have ignored Western sanctions, such as China, India, Turkey and the UAE.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_sanctions_during_the_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"places":[{"title":"United States","extract":"The United States of America (USA), also known as the United States (U.S.) or America, is a country primarily located in North America. It is a federal republic consisting of 50 states and a federal capital district, Washington, D.C. The 48 contiguous states border Canada to the north and Mexico to the south, with the semi-exclave of Alaska in the northwest and the archipelago of Hawaii in the Pacific Ocean. The United States also asserts sovereignty over five major island territories and various uninhabited islands in Oceania and the Caribbean. It is a megadiverse country, with the world's fourth-largest total area and third-largest population, exceeding 341 million.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"US"},{"title":"Russia","extract":"Russia, or the Russian Federation, is a country in Eastern Europe and North Asia. It is the largest country in the world, spanning eleven time zones and sharing land borders with fourteen countries. With a population of over 140 million, Russia is the most populous country in Europe and the ninth-most populous in the world. It is a highly urbanised country, with three-fourths of its population living in urban areas. Moscow, the most populous metropolitan area in Europe, is the capital and largest city of Russia, while Saint Petersburg is its second-largest city and a major cultural centre.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"RU"}],"arc":{"reports":152,"first_seen":"2026-10-09T21:16:00Z","first_title":"Trump strikes diesel deal with Putin , US lifts sanctions | Rediff - TV","first_url":"https://tv.rediff.com/news/trump-strikes-diesel-deal-with-putin-us-lifts-sanctions/407754","first_publisher":"tv.rediff.com","earlier":[{"id":"e_51c4332e478c","title":"Zelenskyy warns US’ Russia sanctions relief could reward Putin and fuel more attacks","date":"2026-10-17T13:23:59Z","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","publisher":"TRT World","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_a2941e0d1300","title":"World in Brief: Fresh protests flare up across France; Trump waives sanctions on Russia","date":"2026-10-17T13:56:39Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxQSTN5UG9GYV9PU2J5dXlPaW9ZdllSaU9YZHhCSjhwb3pLLTkwNW9Sck9feWtjSmE3WW5EYnNabWNJWlZKcnA4SDFuMnBLcDRNUUZQLXlKaG9BTXFuV3JUbTVBQW5EdGNiQWxCNm9lanZlbWllS3RhbnF2S2tmc0h5ckM0djR1bHdkbGZraEpLM29Zc1Eyempv?oc=5","publisher":"The Economist","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_ea3fc33a2192","title":"Trump Russia Sanctions Waiver Makes Tariff Threat Lose Its Bite","date":"2026-10-17T14:45:00Z","url":"https://sputnikglobe.com/20261017/trumps-russia-sanctions-waiver-makes-tariff-thre